  "caveats": [
    "Distance is PER TRACK, not per player: a fragmented identity appears as several short runners. Check track_seconds before comparing players.",
    "Only calibrated frames contribute, so distance UNDERCOUNTS whenever coverage is below 100% (here 79.7%). Values are not scaled up.",
    "140 displacement(s) implying more than 10.0 m/s were dropped as tracking or calibration jitter.",
    "Top speed is a straight-line average over a 1.0s window, not a single sample. Single-sample speed is meaningless at this sampling rate: two metres of positional noise over 0.2s alone reads as 36 km/h. Averaging also UNDER-reports a genuine curved sprint.",
    "Positions are sampled every 12 frames, so distance along a curved run is slightly under-measured."
